    "result_text": "All 28 tests pass, `BUILD SUCCESS`. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived, read-only `locality` field to the owner response, computed from the city via the fixed city-to-region table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`util/Locality.java`** (new) \u2014 a small helper holding the pinned table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) with `Locality.of(city)` returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any unlisted city.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `locality` read-only property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (matching how `displayName`, `membershipTier`, etc. are declared).\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` deriving `locality` from `owner.getCity()` via `Locality.of(...)`, following the same expression-mapping pattern already used for the other server-derived owner fields.\n\nThe field flows through the existing `RespondWithOwner` / `RespondWithOwnerCreated` steps automatically since they map the entity through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`. The new `Cp17Tests` (known city \u2192 `NSW`, unknown city \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) pass, and all 28 acceptance tests remain green.",
